SUMMARY:Deadline: Culture Push: Fellowship for Utopian Practice 2027 (New Y
 ork City)
DESCRIPTION:Culture Push\, the New York nonprofit founded by artists to sup
 port hybrid art and civic experimental practice\, selects 6 to 8 fellows p
 er cycle for its yearlong Fellowship for Utopian Practice. The fellowship 
 backs boundary-pushing\, socially engaged projects that are new and withou
 t prior institutional support. WHAT YOU GET: a USD 2\,250 stipend\, fiscal
  sponsorship for fundraising\, and structured feedback and mentoring acros
 s the year. ELIGIBILITY: minimum of three years of experience\; currently 
 enrolled undergraduates cannot apply\; group and collaborative proposals a
 re welcome\; project work must take place within the five boroughs and fel
 lows must live within commuting distance of New York City (not strictly NY
 C residents). The same deadline also covers the 2027 Black Utopian Fellows
 hip\, Disability Arts + Dreaming Fellowship\, and Climate Justice Fellowsh
 ip. DEADLINE: 15 October 2026 at 11:59 pm ET. Fellowship runs January to D
 ecember 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Culture Push\nLocation: New York City\, US.
  Project work must occur within the five boroughs and fellows must live wi
 thin commuting distance of NYC.\nAward: USD 2\,250 stipend\, plus fiscal s
 ponsorship for fundraising\, feedback and mentoring. No application fee.\n
 Duration: One calendar year\, January to December 2027.\n\nMore: https://w
 ww.culturepush.org/guidelines?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://www.culturepush.org/guidelines?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York City\, US. Project work must occur within the five boroug
 hs and fellows must live within commuting distance of NYC.
END:VEVENT
