SUMMARY:Deadline: Culture Push: Climate Justice Fellowship 2027 (New York C
 ity)
DESCRIPTION:Culture Push's yearlong Climate Justice Fellowship invites arti
 sts\, researchers and activists to develop community-based projects explor
 ing the intersection of climate change and urban socio-political life in N
 ew York City\, across site-specific geographies and topics such as technol
 ogy\, housing\, parks\, urban forests\, food systems\, watersheds\, pollut
 ion and infrastructures. The Fellowship for Utopian Practice is the umbrel
 la program and the same guidelines apply: a USD 2\,250 stipend\, fiscal sp
 onsorship\, mentoring\, and access to Materials for the Arts. ELIGIBILITY:
  at least 3 years of experience\; currently enrolled undergraduates cannot
  apply\; group proposals welcome\; projects must be new\, socially engaged
 \, without prior institutional support (pre-existing performances\, establ
 ished projects and fully funded works are not eligible)\, and grounded in 
 a specific NYC neighborhood or community\; fellows must live within commut
 ing distance of New York City. Applicants may apply to only one Culture Pu
 sh fellowship per cycle\; unselected themed applications pass into the Gen
 eral Fellowship pool. DEADLINE: 15 October 2026 at 11:59 pm ET.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Culture Push\nLocation: New York City\, US. Project work must occur
  within the five boroughs and fellows must live within commuting distance 
 of NYC.\nAward: USD 2\,250 stipend\, plus fiscal sponsorship for fundraisi
 ng\, mentorship and strategizing support\, per the umbrella Fellowship for
  Utopian Practice guidelines. No application fee.\nDuration: One calendar 
 year\, January to December 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.culturepush.org/2027
 -climate-justice-fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
