UID:andrew-carnegie-fellows-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T015915Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261113
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261114
SUMMARY:Deadline: Andrew Carnegie Fellows Program 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Andrew Carnegie Fellows Program awards USD 200\,000 each to
  scholars\, journalists\, authors and public intellectuals for one to two 
 years of research and writing toward a book or major study in the social s
 ciences and humanities\, with recent classes framed around understanding U
 S political polarization and strengthening social cohesion. HOW IT WORKS: 
 this is a nomination-based program\; individuals cannot apply directly. No
 minations come from designated nominators at universities\, colleges\, thi
 nk tanks\, publishers and other institutions\, and most nominating institu
 tions run internal selection rounds with deadlines in early October 2026 (
 check your institution's research office). Carnegie Corporation's nominati
 on deadline is 13 November 2026\, with fellows announced in spring 2027. E
 LIGIBILITY: US-based candidates put forward by their institutions\; both s
 enior and junior scholars are considered. If you are affiliated with a uni
 versity or think tank and want to be considered\, contact your institution
 's limited-submissions or research development office well before its inte
 rnal deadline. NOMINATION DEADLINE: 13 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Car
 negie Corporation of New York\nLocation: US. For US-based scholars\, journ
 alists\, authors and public intellectuals\; candidates must be nominated b
 y their institution (direct applications are not accepted).\nAward: USD 20
 0\,000 over one to two years for research and writing toward a book or maj
 or study. NOTE: institutional nomination required\; individuals cannot app
 ly directly.\nDuration: One to two years of funded research and writing.\n
 \nMore: https://carnegie.org/our-work/special-projects/andrew-carnegie-fel
 lows/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://carnegie.org/our-work/special-projects/andrew-carnegie-fellows/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:US. For US-based scholars\, journalists\, authors and public intel
 lectuals\; candidates must be nominated by their institution (direct appli
 cations are not accepted).
END:VEVENT
