SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council New York Fellowship 2027 (USD 38\,
 000)
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's New York Fellowship brings artists
 \, scholars and arts professionals from Asia to New York City for a six-mo
 nth immersive cultural exchange. SUPPORT: USD 38\,000 for the six-month fe
 llowship. ELIGIBILITY: non-US citizens/residents from ACC-eligible Asian c
 ountries (including Bangladesh\, Cambodia\, China\, Hong Kong\, India\, In
 donesia\, Japan\, Korea\, Malaysia\, Mongolia\, Myanmar\, Nepal\, Pakistan
 \, Philippines\, Singapore\, Sri Lanka\, Taiwan\, Thailand and Vietnam\, a
 mong others)\; age 21+\; at least five years of professional experience in
  an eligible discipline (architecture\, archaeology\, art history\, arts a
 dministration\, arts criticism\, conservation\, crafts\, curation\, dance\
 , ethnomusicology\, film\, literature\, museum studies\, music\, theater\,
  visual art)\; English proficiency (J-1 visa requirement)\; fellows cannot
  work or pursue coursework during the fellowship. COHORTS: January-June 20
 28 or July-December 2028. HOW TO APPLY: via the GoApply platform\; applica
 tions open 1 October 2026. Recommendation letters due 16 November 2026. No
  application fee. DEADLINE: 10 November 2026 at 9:59 AM ET.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Asian Cultural Council\nLocation: Six-month fellowship in New York City
 . For artists\, scholars and arts professionals from ACC-eligible Asian co
 untries (non-US citizens/residents).\nAward: USD 38\,000 for the six-month
  fellowship\, covering the immersive cultural exchange in New York City. N
 o application fee.\nDuration: Six months\, in one of two cohorts: January-
 June 2028 or July-December 2028\n\nMore: https://www.asianculturalcouncil.
 org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Six-month fellowship in New York City. For artists\, scholars and 
 arts professionals from ACC-eligible Asian countries (non-US citizens/resi
 dents).
END:VEVENT
