SUMMARY:Deadline: The Center Fellowship for Justice-Impacted Artists (Cente
 r for Art & Advocacy\, US)
DESCRIPTION:The Center Fellowship (formerly Right of Return)\, run by The C
 enter for Art & Advocacy\, supports formerly incarcerated artists with an 
 annual award of USD 10\,000 in unrestricted funds and USD 10\,000 in proje
 ct development funds. ELIGIBILITY: open to any directly justice-impacted\,
  US-based artist working in visual art\, film\, music\, creative writing\,
  performance\, design\, or other multidisciplinary practice\, regardless o
 f citizenship status\, felony convictions\, or formal training in the arts
 . WHAT YOU GET: beyond the USD 20\,000 in combined funding\, fellows are i
 nvited to an annual retreat to network with previous fellows\, advocates\,
  industry leaders\, and funders\, where they can present project proposals
 \, receive peer feedback\, and attend New York City cultural events. APPLI
 CATION: via Submittable (linked from the programs page)\; program inquirie
 s to outreach@thecenter.art. DEADLINE: 25 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: T
 he Center for Art & Advocacy\nLocation: USA. Open to US-based\, directly j
 ustice-impacted artists regardless of citizenship status\, felony convicti
 ons\, or formal arts training.\nAward: USD 10\,000 in unrestricted funds p
 lus USD 10\,000 in project development funds per fellow\, awarded annually
 .\nDuration: One-year fellowship cohort\, including an annual retreat with
  previous fellows\, advocates\, industry leaders\, and funders.\n\nMore: h
 ttps://centerforartandadvocacy.org/programs?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral#fellowship
URL:https://centerforartandadvocacy.org/programs?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral#fellowship
LOCATION:USA. Open to US-based\, directly justice-impacted artists regardle
 ss of citizenship status\, felony convictions\, or formal arts training.
