SUMMARY:Deadline: Paul & Daisy Soros Fellowships for New Americans 2027 (US
  graduate study)
DESCRIPTION:The Paul & Daisy Soros Fellowships for New Americans annually s
 elect 30 fellows based on their potential to make significant contribution
 s to American society\, culture\, and their chosen fields\, across discipl
 ines including the arts. WHAT YOU GET: up to USD 90\,000 over two years in
  stipend and tuition support for graduate study beginning fall 2027\, plus
  mentorship\, community\, all-expenses-paid attendance at the Fall Confere
 nce\, and lifelong connection to a network of nearly 900 fellows. ELIGIBIL
 ITY: applicants must be an immigrant or the child of immigrant(s)\, meet t
 he program's age requirements\, and be in the first two years of a graduat
 e or professional program or applying to one during the admissions process
 \; school selectivity\, GPA\, and test scores are not used to determine el
 igibility\, and reapplying is allowed. APPLICATION: free\, via the online 
 portal\, with a resume or CV\, two essays (1\,000 words max each)\, transc
 ripts\, any program-required test scores\, and 3 to 5 recommendation lette
 rs. TIMELINE: finalists notified mid-January 2027\, virtual interviews in 
 February\, winners notified in March. DEADLINE: 29 October 2026\, 2:00 PM 
 EDT.\n\nOrganisation: The Paul & Daisy Soros Fellowships for New Americans
 \nLocation: USA. For immigrants and children of immigrants pursuing gradua
 te or professional study at US institutions.\nAward: Up to USD 90\,000 ove
 r two years (stipend and tuition support) toward graduate study\; 30 fello
 wships awarded annually. No application fee.\nDuration: Two years of fundi
 ng for graduate study\, beginning fall 2027\, plus all-expenses-paid atten
 dance at the Fall Conference.\n\nMore: https://pdsoros.org/application-pro
 cess/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://pdsoros.org/application-process/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:USA. For immigrants and children of immigrants pursuing graduate o
 r professional study at US institutions.
END:VEVENT
